WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:05.710
Hey guys, it's Jan here, I was super-psyched
to see the first part of the Daredevil Season

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:10.559
2 trailer which gives us a great look at the
conflict between Frank Castle, aka the Punisher,

00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:11.660
and Matt Murdock's Daredevil.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:15.960
So, I wanted to break down the trailer and
explain some of the easter eggs and references.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:19.610
Just before I get stuck in, there will be
potential spoilers for season 2.

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:23.850
If you want to avoid those spoilers and get
a refresher for season 1, check out my video

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:26.330
15 Things You Probably Didn't Know About Daredevil.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:31.320
Ok, this trailer is definitely all about establishing
the Punisher's origin story.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.050
After a shot of Castle's home and pictures
of his family we get this interesting shot

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.760
of him sitting in front of what looks like
New York's Central Park Carousel with the

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.850
lights clicking off one by one.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:45.079
This, along with the creepy sound of a child
singing, is likely a nod to how Frank Castle

00:00:45.079 --> 00:00:48.730
lost his wife and children in the comics when
they were gunned down by mobsters in Central

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:49.730
Park.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:53.429
There's more hints that this location is significant
later in the trailer with Punisher taking

00:00:53.429 --> 00:00:55.739
out some bad guys at the carousel in this
shot.

00:00:55.739 --> 00:01:00.589
The x-ray of the skull that Karen is handling
is an easter egg for The Punisher's signature

00:01:00.589 --> 00:01:02.989
white skull we see on his comic book costume.

00:01:02.989 --> 00:01:07.250
But look a bit closer at the shot from the
trailer and you'll also see Karen's fingers

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:12.329
run just behind a dark circle to the left
of the skull, a likely reference to the bullet

00:01:12.329 --> 00:01:16.030
wound Frank Castle suffered to his head during
the mob attack which killed his family.

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:20.229
Also there in the background are what look
like case files that Karen might be going

00:01:20.229 --> 00:01:24.469
over and there seems to be a bloodied victim
in one of the photos with meat hanging around

00:01:24.469 --> 00:01:29.090
him which ties in with this set photo of Daredevil
standing in what looks like a meat packing

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:30.090
warehouse.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:33.950
And it's possibly a nod to the fact that in
Punisher's extended world of comics, video

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:38.850
games, and movies, he's used equipment like
meat hooks and grinders or even meat itself

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:44.590
to deal with opponents for example in the
Streets of Laredo comics, the 1989 and 2004

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:48.770
Punisher movies, and the 2005 Punisher video
game which features a meat packing plant.

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:53.409
And the trailer also alludes to the Punisher's
military past in the comic books when we see

00:01:53.409 --> 00:01:57.979
some of his weapons, which he has tons of
in the comics, and when we hear the words

00:01:57.979 --> 00:02:01.179
about how he's taking out gangs with "military
precision".

00:02:01.179 --> 00:02:05.420
In the comics, Frank Castle spent time in
the Marines, four years in Vietnam and also

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:07.460
ran black ops missions.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:12.120
The "One Batch, Two Batch" book likely belonged
to Castle's child, but given that the show's

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:16.730
production designer and showrunner could have
chosen anything to illustrate the front cover,

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:21.040
the fact they chose bears feels like a nod
to the time the Punisher used a group of polar

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:24.140
bears in a zoo to attack the Gnucci crime
family.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:28.930
And, given Castle's military background, the
phrase "one batch, two batch" might be a reference

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:32.981
to the Jessica Jones character Will Simpson,
who is the MCU's version of the comic book

00:02:32.981 --> 00:02:37.980
character Frank Simpson, aka Nuke, who underwent
a super-soldier program similar to the one

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.900
which created Captain America.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:44.830
Simpson's medication consists of one red pill
to get him going, two white to keep him even

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:47.150
and one blue to bring him down.

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:50.520
Will Simpson has a military background and
the show implies what he went through made

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:54.709
him unstable and it'll be interesting to see
if there's any connection in this shared universe

00:02:54.709 --> 00:02:56.310
between him and Castle.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:03:01.010
The Punisher's phrase "penny and dime" as
he goes to take a shot could be a nod to the

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:05.900
comic book title "Ten To One" from the Punisher
War Journal series and the number 10 also

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:09.910
seems significant given there's a number 10
card we can spot later at the scene of a massacre.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:13.720
Or it could be a reference to the 'penny and
dime' trick where a penny is used to make

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:17.840
a dime disappear, which in this case would
mean the Punisher is making a group of bad

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:18.910
guys disappear.

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:23.580
While Matt's discussing his Catholic guilt
with Father Lantom, we glimpse a crucifix

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:28.460
and what could be a nun's habit, a hint perhaps
that Matt returns to meet a nun at St Agnes'

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:29.460
Orphanage.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:34.160
We saw the orphanage run by nuns briefly in
a season 1 flashback scene to Matt's childhood

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:35.430
where he met Stick.

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:39.319
In the comic books, we learn that Matt's mother
Maggie became a nun called Margaret, so it'll

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:42.079
be interesting to see if Matt meets her this
season.

00:03:42.079 --> 00:03:45.860
By the way, this is the same orphanage that
Skye from Agents of SHIELD grew up in.

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:50.020
The DA's office gets a mention in the trailer
and seems to be passing information on to

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:55.209
Matt Murdock, a likely nod to the new season
2 character Blake Tower played by Stephen

00:03:55.209 --> 00:03:56.209
Rider.

00:03:56.209 --> 00:03:59.740
In the comics, Blake Tower is New York's district
attorney and helps Daredevil catch various

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:00.780
criminals.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:04.400
There's quite a bit of interaction between
Matt Murdock and Karen Page in this trailer

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.690
and a hint at a likely romance between them.

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:09.920
In the comics, Karen is one of Matt's longest-running
love interests.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:14.640
There are some fast-cut rooftop scenes with
Daredevil and The Punisher arguing.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:18.440
One of the shots shows Daredevil up against
some bricks, which is likely the same moment

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:21.880
from this set photo in which The Punisher
has chained up Daredevil.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:26.620
It's an iconic moment in the comics where
Daredevil finds himself in a Sophie's Choice

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:27.620
situation.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:30.820
Daredevil disagrees with the Punisher taking
out criminals and believes they need to be

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:32.720
arrested and punished by the law.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:37.190
Punisher is about to kill Dino Gnucci, a member
of a prominent crime family, and gives Daredevil

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:42.210
a gun telling him the only way to stop him
shooting Gnucci is to kill the Punisher himself.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:47.430
In either case, Daredevil has to murder or
let someone be murdered.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:51.620
It's a really great scene and later in the
comics the Punisher sets Daredevil free after

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:56.090
knocking him out, which is likely why we see
him later in the trailer using a chain to

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:57.970
fight in a couple of shots.

00:04:57.970 --> 00:05:02.440
The Punisher's line to Daredevil "you're one
bad day away from being me" goes back to the

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:07.139
Daredevil comics and also reminds me of The
Joker's "one bad day" line in the Batman comic

00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:08.139
The Killing Joke.

00:05:08.139 --> 00:05:11.740
We also get a look at two different Daredevil
masks in the trailer.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:15.740
Here we see the same red mask he had at the
end of Season 1, and later he's wearing a

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:16.940
black mask.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:21.130
The black mask is damaged in this shot, but
it matches the black mask in one of the official

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:22.130
set photos.

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:27.190
And to cap off the awesome trailer, we get
an introduction to Elodie Yung's Elektra who

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:28.720
we see already knows Matt.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:33.100
There was a reference to her in season 1 when
Foggy asked Matt about the Greek girl he dated

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:36.240
in college and Matt said that it didn't work
out between them.

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:40.289
In the comics, Elektra is the daughter of
a Greek ambassador, is trained in martial

00:05:40.289 --> 00:05:42.770
arts, and has had an on-off relationship with
Matt Murdock.

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:47.300
Now, I'll have more discussion of Elektra
in my video about Part 2 of the trailer, but

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:51.960
it's worth pointing out that we didn't get
to see Wilson Fisk return yet in this trailer.

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:57.160
I'm hopeful he will be in season 2 as he hires
Elektra as a bodyguard in the comics to protect

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:58.759
himself against the Punisher.

00:05:58.759 --> 00:06:02.510
So what other easter eggs did you spot in
the trailer and what do you think about Jon

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:04.300
Bernthal as The Punisher?

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:05.960
Let me know in the comments below.

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:09.819
Next week I'll have another breakdown and
easter egg review of the part 2 trailer, so

00:06:09.819 --> 00:06:12.080
do make sure you're subscribed to get that.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:15.949
And in the meantime, you can also take a look
at some of my other videos including 15 cool

00:06:15.949 --> 00:06:20.050
behind-the-scenes facts about the making of
Daredevil, Jessica Jones season 1 easter eggs,

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:21.740
and Deadpool easter eggs.

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:22.740
Thanks for watching!

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:26.950
Yippee ki-yay movie lovers!

